  <RoyalTitleDef ParentName="BaseNephilimEmpireTitleNPC">
    <defName>NephilimDuchess</defName>
    <label>nephilim duchess</label>
    <labelFemale>nephilim duchess</labelFemale>
    <description>The Nephilim title of duchess is the highest of the middle nobility.\n\nIn the Nephilim Empire, duchesses control provinces, mega-gardens, or moons. At war, a duke can field a division-level force, or a fleet with capital ships an dozens of support craft.</description>
    <seniority>705</seniority>
    <commonality>1</commonality>	
  </RoyalTitleDef>

  <RoyalTitleDef ParentName="BaseNephilimEmpireTitleNPC">
    <defName>NephilimConsul</defName>
    <label>nephilim consul</label>
    <description>Nephilim Consuls are Maidens, Handmaidens, and humanoid sympathizers who have proven themselves invaluable to the Nephilim Empire but are, for one reason or another, not qualified for Grand Matronhood.\n\nThese individuals occupy the highest rank that can be achieved in the Nephilim government without at least achieving Grand Matronhood.</description>
    <seniority>805</seniority>
    <commonality>0.6</commonality>	
  </RoyalTitleDef>

  <RoyalTitleDef ParentName="BaseNephilimEmpireTitleNPC">
    <defName>NephilimGrandMatronTitle</defName>
    <label>grand matron</label>
    <description>Nephilim Grand Matrons are the undisputed rulers of the Nephilim. While Ascended Matrons technically hold the highest rank in the hierarchy, their insane physical circumstances and hyperfecundity leave them too self-absorbed and mind-blasted to effectively rule an empire. The Grand Matrons, though swollen near to the point of immobility, are still able to lord over those beneath them, organizing the affairs of a galactice empire through mouths filled with delectable foods and lustful moans.</description>
    <seniority>905</seniority>
    <rewards>
	<PsychicAmplifier>1</PsychicAmplifier>	  
    </rewards>	
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>	
  </RoyalTitleDef>

  <!-- Emperor should never appear in the game in any way, it's just here for completeness on UI lists etc. -->
  <RoyalTitleDef ParentName="BaseNephilimEmpireTitleNPC">
    <defName>NephilimAscendedMatron</defName>
    <label>ascended matron</label>
    <labelFemale>ascended matron</labelFemale>
    <description>An ascended matron is a Nephilim Grand Matron who has absorbed the planet she was birthed on. As much stellar object as goo girl, ascended matrons exist at the top of the Nephilim hierarchy, churning out huge quantities of mechanite infused "star ships" to spearhead Nephilim armadas. \n\nAscended Matronhood is the ideal of all Nephilim, and new Nephilim colonies will seek to conquer the world they are on so that one of their own can ascend as quickly as possible.</description>
    <seniority>1005</seniority>
    <commonality>0.0</commonality>
  </RoyalTitleDef>

